- New functions (append):

```ts
/**
 * Adds one tag to a closet's outfit tags and returns the whole saved list.
 * Done in the `add_closet_outfit_label` RPC rather than by writing the array
 * from here, so a device holding an older copy of the list can't overwrite a
 * tag added elsewhere in the meantime. Caller must own the closet. Throws the
 * Supabase error on failure.
 */
export async function addClosetOutfitLabel(closetId: string, label: string): Promise<string[]> {
  const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('add_closet_outfit_label', {
    target_closet_id: closetId,
    target_label: label,
  });
  if (error) throw error;
  return data;
}

/**
 * Removes one tag from a closet's outfit tags and returns the whole saved
 * list - see addClosetOutfitLabel for why this is an RPC. Outfits that
 * already carry the tag are not changed. Caller must own the closet. Throws
 * the Supabase error on failure.
 */
export async function removeClosetOutfitLabel(closetId: string, label: string): Promise<string[]> {
  const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('remove_closet_outfit_label', {
    target_closet_id: closetId,
    target_label: label,
  });
  if (error) throw error;
  return data;
}
```

Wire format (for mocks/tests): POST /rest/v1/rpc/add_closet_outfit_label with body {"target_closet_id":"<uuid>","target_label":"Vintage"} returns a JSON array of strings; a raised exception returns HTTP 400 {"code":"P0001","message":"You already have a tag called \"Casual\""} which getErrorMessage (dataService.types.ts:456-467) turns into the alert text.

