ClosetContextValue (:8-26) gains:

```ts
  /** Outfit tags of the active closet in display order - the filter pills on the Outfits tab and the Tag select on the create-outfit form. Empty while the closet is loading, or when its owner has removed them all. */
  activeClosetLabels: readonly string[];
  /** Adds a tag to the user's own closet (My Closet mode only) and returns it as saved (trimmed, inner whitespace collapsed). Throws with a user-facing message if it is empty, too long, a duplicate, or the closet is at the tag limit. */
  addOutfitLabel: (label: string) => Promise<string>;
  /** Removes a tag from the user's own closet (My Closet mode only). Outfits that already carry it are left as they are. */
  removeOutfitLabel: (label: string) => Promise<void>;
```

Mutators, placed after regeneratePassphrase (:116-120):

```ts
  const addOutfitLabel = async (label: string): Promise<string> => {
    if (closetMode !== 'my-closet' || !myCloset) throw new Error('Only the closet owner can edit tags.');
    const normalized = normalizeOutfitLabel(label);
    if (!normalized) throw new Error('Enter a tag name.');
    if (normalized.length > MAX_OUTFIT_LABEL_LENGTH) {
      throw new Error(`Tags can be up to ${MAX_OUTFIT_LABEL_LENGTH} characters.`);
    }
    const existing = myCloset.outfit_labels.find(candidate => candidate.toLowerCase() === normalized.toLowerCase());
    if (existing) throw new Error(`You already have a tag called "${existing}".`);
    if (myCloset.outfit_labels.length >= MAX_OUTFIT_LABELS) {
      throw new Error(`You can have up to ${MAX_OUTFIT_LABELS} tags. Remove one to add another.`);
    }

    const closetId = myCloset.closet_id;
    const labels = await dataService.addClosetOutfitLabel(closetId, normalized);
    // The service returns the whole saved list, so this also picks up tags
    // added from another device since the closet was loaded. Matched by id in
    // case the closet was cleared or reloaded while the request was in flight.
    setMyCloset(current => (current?.closet_id === closetId ? { ...current, outfit_labels: labels } : current));
    return normalized;
  };

  const removeOutfitLabel = async (label: string): Promise<void> => {
    if (closetMode !== 'my-closet' || !myCloset) throw new Error('Only the closet owner can edit tags.');
    const closetId = myCloset.closet_id;
    const labels = await dataService.removeClosetOutfitLabel(closetId, label);
    setMyCloset(current => (current?.closet_id === closetId ? { ...current, outfit_labels: labels } : current));
  };
```

Value object (:135-150): add `activeClosetLabels: activeCloset?.outfit_labels ?? NO_LABELS, addOutfitLabel, removeOutfitLabel,`. The useMemo dependency array (:151-162) needs NO change: closetMode, activeCloset, myCloset and dataService are already listed and are everything the new members read.

Why context and not a dirty flag: both consumers (OutfitsGrid, CreateOutfitForm) stay mounted while the user is on the Settings tab; a context value re-renders both at once, whereas consumeOutfitsDirty (src/state/outfitsRefresh.ts:12-16) clears on first read. markOutfitsDirty is NOT called: no outfit row changes.

