Why a separate provider keyed by closet id: the Edit tags screen edits the OWN closet while the grid and the create form read the ACTIVE closet, and those differ in stylist mode. Tabs and pushed screens stay mounted (src/app/(tabs)/_layout.web.tsx:39-55), so an edit must reach them through shared state. The single-consumer dirty flag in src/state/outfitsRefresh.ts:12-16 cannot serve two readers.

```ts
type LabelsEntry = {
  /** Last successfully loaded list; kept while a refresh is in flight or after one fails. Null until the first success. */
  labels: ClosetOutfitLabel[] | null;
  /** Message from the most recent failed load; cleared by the next success. */
  error: string | null;
};

type OutfitLabelsContextValue = {
  entries: Readonly<Record<string, LabelsEntry>>;
  /** Loads a closet's tags into the store. Resolves the fresh list, or null if the load failed (the error is stored). Never rejects. */
  refresh: (closetId: string) => Promise<ClosetOutfitLabel[] | null>;
  addLabel: (closetId: string, name: string) => Promise<ClosetOutfitLabel>;
  removeLabel: (label: ClosetOutfitLabel) => Promise<void>;
};

export function OutfitLabelsProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }): JSX.Element;
/** Throws 'useOutfitLabels must be used within an OutfitLabelsProvider'. */
export function useOutfitLabels(): OutfitLabelsContextValue;
/** One closet's tags. Loads on mount, when closetId changes and every time the calling screen regains focus. */
export function useClosetOutfitLabels(closetId: string | null): {
  labels: ClosetOutfitLabel[] | null;
  error: string | null;
  refresh: () => Promise<ClosetOutfitLabel[] | null>;
};
```
Required behaviour:
- State: entries in useState; a per-closet sequence counter in a ref: `const seq = useRef<Record<string, number>>({})`.
- refresh(closetId): take ticket = ++seq.current[closetId]; await dataService.getClosetOutfitLabels(closetId). Store the result only if seq.current[closetId] === ticket (a newer load or a mutation has not superseded it), but return the fetched list either way. On failure store { labels: previous labels, error: getErrorMessage(err, 'Failed to load tags.') } under the same ticket rule and resolve null.
- addLabel: await dataService.addClosetOutfitLabel; then ++seq.current[closetId] (so a load that started before the insert cannot overwrite the new row), append the returned label to the entry if its id is not already there, start refresh(closetId) without awaiting, return the label. On DuplicateOutfitLabelError also start refresh(closetId) (the list is stale), then rethrow.
- removeLabel: await dataService.removeClosetOutfitLabel(label); ++seq; filter the label out by id; start refresh(label.closet_id) without awaiting.
- refresh, addLabel and removeLabel are useCallback([dataService]); the value is useMemo([entries, refresh, addLabel, removeLabel]). refresh MUST be referentially stable, because the hook puts it in a useFocusEffect dependency list.
- Reset on identity change: useEffect(() => { seq.current = {}; setEntries({}); }, [dataService, userId]) with userId = useAuth().session?.user.id ?? ''. One user's lists are never shown to the next user or across guest/live.
- useClosetOutfitLabels: `useFocusEffect(useCallback(() => { if (closetId) void refresh(closetId); }, [closetId, refresh]))` (useFocusEffect from expo-router); returns the entry for closetId (or { labels: null, error: null }) and a bound refresh that resolves null when closetId is null.
- Mount in src/app/_layout.tsx directly inside <ClosetProvider> (line 62), wrapping <AppShell>. It must sit under DataModeProvider (line 57) and above the Stack, for the reason given in the comment at lines 58-61.

8. src/context/ClosetContext.tsx: NO change. Tags are not carried on StylistCloset/OwnCloset: stylist closets are only refetched when closetMode flips (ClosetContext.tsx:77-97), which would freeze an owner's tag edits out of a stylist's running session, and the hand-maintained useMemo dependency list (lines 151-162) is a known trap. The own closet for Edit tags is fetched directly (see whoCanEdit).

